Core: Scripts in tags using the Groovy part type are now checked for compilation errors when they are saved. If a script does not compile, saving fails with "400 Bad Request" and an error message naming the node and the line, column and reason of the error. Classes from Groovy scripts of devtool packages can be imported, if the package is assigned to the node. The script must compile in every node, in which it can be used (e.g. all nodes a template is assigned to).
